                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I can't give this game a strong enough recommendation. I love the Creeper World series, so I tried this out because it is a spin-off in the same universe, but I ended up absolutely loving it on its own merits. The gameplay is essentially a mix of RTS and tower defence, where the enemy is a particulate which, to some degree, acts like a liquid. The \"towers\" are mobile spaceships, which all serve different functions, and the campaign is excellent, as is the soundtrack.\n\nHowever, where this game really shines is the custom content. There is an absolutely gigantic database of player-created levels to play, and the spaceship system is incredibly versatile which really adds to these. Ships serve different functions, as mentioned, but the ships are made up of different combinations of blocks, and really, it is these blocks which have the functions, not the ship as such. Because of this, custom levels can also have completely custom fleets, and in many levels, you will be adapting not only to the terrain the creator has made for you, but also sometimes a completely unfamiliar set of ships which are tailored to the level itself. Overall an amazing game.",
